---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — Finora"
  description="Finora Privacy Policy. Learn how we handle your data, sessions, and research queries."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16 md:px-8 md:py-24">
    <div>
      <p class="font-mono text-caption-mono uppercase tracking-wide text-accent">// legal</p>
      <h1 class="mt-4 text-display-lg text-ink">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-body-sm text-mute">Last updated: August 28, 2026</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose mt-10 space-y-8 text-body-md text-body leading-relaxed">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">1. Introduction</h2>
        <p>
          This Privacy Policy explains how Finora Labs ("we", "us") collects, uses, and protects
          information when you use the Finora financial research platform ("the Service").
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">2. Information We Collect</h2>

        <h3 class="mt-4 text-body-md-strong text-ink">Account Information</h3>
        <p>
          When you create an account, we collect your email address, name, and a hashed version of your
          password. We do not store plaintext passwords.
        </p>

        <h3 class="mt-4 text-body-md-strong text-ink">Authentication &amp; Session Data</h3>
        <p>
          We maintain session tokens to keep you logged in. These tokens are stored locally in your
          browser and expire after a period of inactivity.
        </p>

        <h3 class="mt-4 text-body-md-strong text-ink">Research Queries</h3>
        <p>
          When you research a company, we store the research parameters (company name, time period,
          objective) and the resulting research session data. This includes extracted financial statements,
          calculated metrics, source documents, and verification results.
        </p>

        <h3 class="mt-4 text-body-md-strong text-ink">Chat Messages</h3>
        <p>
          Chat messages are processed in real-time and are not permanently stored on our servers.
          Conversation history is maintained only during your active session.
        </p>

        <h3 class="mt-4 text-body-md-strong text-ink">Usage Counters</h3>
        <p>
          We track research run counts and daily chat message counts per user to enforce usage limits.
          These counters reset automatically.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-inside list-disc space-y-2 pl-4">
          <li>To provide and improve the research and analysis features</li>
          <li>To enforce usage limits and prevent abuse</li>
          <li>To authenticate your identity and maintain your session</li>
          <li>To troubleshoot technical issues</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">4. Third-Party Services</h2>
        <p>
          Finora processes data through the following third-party services to provide its features:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-inside list-disc space-y-2 pl-4">
          <li><strong class="text-ink">SEC EDGAR</strong> — Public financial filing data (10-K, 10-Q, XBRL)</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ink">NVIDIA API</strong> — AI language model processing for chat and summaries</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ink">Twelve Data</strong> — Stock market price data</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ink">Tavily</strong> — Web search for source discovery</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ink">Jina</strong> — Web page content extraction</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Each third-party service has its own privacy policy. We encourage you to review their policies.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">5. Cookies &amp; Storage</h2>
        <p>
          Finora uses local storage to maintain your authentication session and theme preferences.
          We do not use tracking cookies or analytics cookies. The only stored items are:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-inside list-disc space-y-2 pl-4">
          <li><code class="rounded bg-canvas-soft px-1.5 py-0.5 text-code">finora-auth-token</code> — Your session token</li>
          <li><code class="rounded bg-canvas-soft px-1.5 py-0.5 text-code">finora-theme</code> — Your light/dark theme preference</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">6. Data Security</h2>
        <p>
          We implement reasonable security measures including HTTPS encryption, hashed passwords,
          and input validation. However, no method of electronic storage is 100% secure. We cannot
          guarantee absolute security.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">7. Data Retention</h2>
        <p>
          Research session data is stored for a limited period to allow you to revisit your dashboards.
          Account data is retained as long as your account is active. You may request data deletion
          by contacting us.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">8. Your Responsibilities</h2>
        <p>
          You are responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of your account credentials and for
          all activity that occurs under your account.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">9. Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Changes will be posted on this page
          with an updated date. Your continued use of the Service after changes constitutes acceptance.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">10. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about this Privacy Policy? Contact us at
          <a href="mailto:hello@finora.dev" class="text-accent hover:underline">hello@finora.dev</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
